          "title": "A Walk in the Rain",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "“I think I’ll go for a walk,” I said, looking out at the gray sky. A moment later, rain tapped on the window. I put on my coat and stepped outside anyway. The street was quiet, and little pools of water shone beside the path. I enjoyed the cool air, but soon my hair and sleeves were wet."
            },
            {
              "text": "At the corner, I saw my neighbor, Mrs. Lee, carrying two bags. She had no umbrella, and one bag was tearing. “Would you like some help?” I asked. “That would be kind,” she said with a smile. I held the bag while she tied it with a piece of string. Then she offered me a warm cup of tea at her home."
            },
            {
              "text": "We sat by the window and watched the rain run down the glass. Mrs. Lee told me about her garden and the small birds that came to visit. When the rain grew lighter, I thanked her and walked home. My short walk had turned into a lovely visit, and I was glad I had gone outside."
            }
          ],
