          "revision": 1,
          "title": "A Walk in the Rain",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "Rain began as I left the shop. I had no coat, and the street grew wet and dark. I walked slowly, trying to keep my shoes out of the water. At the corner, my neighbour called to me from her home. “You look cold,” she said. “Would you like to share my umbrella?” I thanked her and walked beside her under it."
            },
            {
              "text": "We went toward home together. She told me about her small garden and the flowers she hoped to plant when the weather was warm. I told her I had seen the red flowers by her gate, and she smiled. Rain tapped above us while cars passed on the road. She asked how long I had lived on the street. “Only a few months,” I said. She was glad to have a new neighbour."
            },
            {
              "text": "At my door, I thanked her again and offered to bring her tea another day. “That sounds lovely,” she said. Before she went home, she made sure I could get inside without getting wet. The walk had started as a cold trip, but it ended with a friendly talk. Now, when I see her, I smile and say hello."
            }
          ],
